course: dictionary
lesson: 7757
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word puppet has two. To find which one the writer means, read the words around it: they are its context, and they leave clues.
explain: «Mia slipped a finger puppet onto her thumb and made it wave.» Here a puppet is a toy you move with your hand. The clues are slipped onto her thumb and made it wave.
explain: «The small country was only a puppet of its powerful neighbour, doing whatever it was told.» Here a puppet is a person or group controlled by someone else. The clue is doing whatever it was told. Always try your meaning in the sentence to check it makes sense.
fact: A puppet is a toy figure of a person or animal that you move with your hand, strings or sticks to act out a show.
fact: A puppet can also be a person or group controlled by someone else, who does what they are told.
fact: Kinds of puppet include hand puppets, glove puppets, finger puppets, string puppets (marionettes) and shadow puppets.
fact: «Condor chicks were fed with puppets shaped like condor heads.» The puppets helped the chicks stay wild, so they would not be raised only by people.
fact: «In The Lion King musical the puppets are designed so you see both the actor and the animal.»
exercise: «Sam wiggled the puppet on his hand, and it nodded at the audience.» What is a puppet in this sentence? | *A toy figure you move with your hand | A tiny stone | A person who fears danger | A ruler controlled by another country
exercise: «The weak king was only a puppet of the powerful neighbour, doing exactly what it said.» What does puppet mean here? | A toy shaped like a condor | A show with music | *A person or group controlled by someone else | A kind of shadow on a wall
exercise: Which kind of puppet fits over one finger? | Shadow puppet | Glove puppet | String puppet | *Finger puppet
test: «The puppet show ended with a big round of applause.» Is puppet a toy or a controlled person here? | A person controlled by another country | A stone on the stage | *A toy, used in a show | A kind of applause
test: «A puppet ruler does what a stronger country tells it to do.» What does puppet ruler mean? | A ruler who makes his own decisions | A ruler who lives in a puppet theatre | A ruler who is very old | *A ruler controlled by another country
exam: «The string puppet danced across the stage, but in the history lesson the puppet king had no power at all.» In each use, which meaning fits? | A toy you move with strings, and then a person controlled by someone else | *A toy you move with strings, and then a person controlled by someone else, in the same sense | A show with music, and then a toy shaped like a condor | A tiny stone, and then a shadow on a wall
